# Pixels of NetSurf on Burrow (W24-S04), dumped by tests/smoke/keys/browser.keys.
# Append-only. NetSurf's 800x600 window at (0,0) on Xfbdev, showing
# tests/smoke/browser-pages.py's index page: the styled box (BOX_RGB), the
# PNG (IMAGE_RGB) and the page's white background on both sides of them.
size  build/screen-browser-page.ppm 1024 768
pixel build/screen-browser-page.ppm 140 200 #20a040
pixel build/screen-browser-page.ppm 48 280 #d03030
pixel build/screen-browser-page.ppm 600 400 #ffffff
pixel build/screen-browser-page.ppm 140 290 #ffffff
# S05: the link clicked with the tablet: the second page's banner (PAGE2_RGB);
# a typed URL, the long page scrolled down three pages to its end block
# (LONG_END_RGB); busybox httpd's page over loopback (LOCAL_RGB); the page
# over TLS with the test CA (SECURE_RGB).
pixel build/screen-browser-second.ppm 400 100 #3050c0
pixel build/screen-browser-scrolled.ppm 400 300 #f08010
pixel build/screen-browser-local.ppm 400 100 #c0a000
pixel build/screen-browser-secure.ppm 400 100 #208080
# S05: the certificate for another name from no known CA: NetSurf's "Privacy
# error" page instead of the TLS page, its "Back to safety" button blue.
pixel build/screen-browser-refused.ppm 600 342 #0060df
pixel build/screen-browser-refused.ppm 400 450 #aaaaaa
